(6695184, 999344, 83313, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ozerad:</b></div><hr/><i> Why are you using mountain bike shoes on a road bike? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Because I like being able to walk. I prefer the type like these that are more roadish, but have some decent tread on the bottoms. The ones with laces in my outtake are MTB shoes that I wear when I am leaving to go riding from work, because I can walk down the stairs and drive my truck with them on.<br/> <br/>Added: Yes, I''m a Fred.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-02-29 12:00:28.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by ozerad: Why are you using mountain bike shoes on a road bike?  Because I like being able to walk. I prefer the type like these that are more roadish, but have some decent tread on the bottoms. The ones with laces in my outtake are MTB shoes that I wear when I am leaving to go riding from work, because I can walk down the stairs and drive my truck with them on. Added: Yes, I''m a Fred.', '2012-02-29 11:52:38.000000', '2012-02-29 12:00:28.000000', 0),
